Email from Ristorante i Ricchi 700 years in the making - now tasting in DC! For over 700 years, the people of Siena have lived for a race that lasts only 90 seconds. Every August, an entire city comes to life in a breathtaking celebration of tradition, rivalry, food, wine, and community. This year, we're bringing that same spirit to i Ricchi for one unforgettable evening.   Did you know? The Palio race lasts just 90 thrilling seconds, but the people of Siena spend the entire year preparing for it. It's far more than a horse race—it's a celebration of family, tradition, rivalry, and community that has united generations for over 700 years. ﻿Join us as we bring a taste of this extraordinary Tuscan tradition to Washington, D.C. for one unforgettable evening.   RESERVE YOUR SPOT ON 8/15!     Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
