Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.     Dear ICS Friends, On Saturday, August 15th, from 11:00 am to 2:30 pm in McLean, Virginia, Ornella will welcome you into her home for a cooking class and guide you through the preparation of three delicious Italian recipes: Pasta alla Norma – One of Sicily’s most famous dishes, a hearty and flavorful pasta made with eggplant and tomato sauce. Sciusceddu Messinese – A traditional dish from Messina, featuring tender meatballs and goat cheese in a rich and comforting preparation. Pizzicotti di Pasta di Mandorle – Traditional Sicilian almond paste cookies. Almonds are one of the region’s signature ingredients, and these small sweets are beloved throughout Sicily. REGISTER (by Thursday night, August 13th) by selecting "Cooking Classes" on the registration page. Visit our website to learn more about this and upcoming culinary events. Buon appetito! The ICS Team       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email   Our Company | Contact Us | FAQs | Privacy Policy   The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
