Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Plus, Palio di Siena Dinner on the 15th! "PALIO DI SIENA DINNER" A Celebration of Tuscany's Oldest Tradition August 15, 2026 MENU (CLICK TO SEE) FOOD + HISTORY + MOVIE = AMAZING NIGHT! Food and entertainment are great diversions. On occasion, it is good to get lost in an old movie especially when it tells the story of man’s past struggles and creative solutions to catastrophic situations. The Secret Life of Santa Vittoria, a delightful classic Italian-American film directed by the legendary Stanley Kramer, is based on a true story of resolve, courage, community spirit, and…one million bottles of wine! It is set in Italy’s beautiful Le Marche region, the backdrop for this week’s authentic late August dinner. Pick up freshly-made dinner from Le Marche, get comfy at home by the TV, open your bottle of red wine from Le Marche (so you can cheer with the protagonist as he saves the same wine from the Nazis!), pull up "Secret of Santa Vittoria" on Prime Video here, and have a gastro-visual delight that will transport you through time and space to the beautiful Marche region of Italy! Le Marche: The Secret of Santa Vittoria WEEK 332 4-COURSE MENU August 4-9, 2026 Insalata di Ceci e Cavolo Rosso Chickpeas, shredded red cabbage, and carrots with sunflower seeds Maccheroncini di Campofilone al Fumè Thin egg pasta, smoked pancetta, and tomato cream Pollo in Potacchio Braised chicken with rosemary and creamy polenta Torta di Susine Fresh black plum tart Featured wine: “Barbarossa” Lacrima di Morro D’Alba, Tenuta Tavignano, 2020 ORDER NOW!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i 