Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.       Dear ICS families, On Monday, August 10, we will begin another enriching week of Italian Summer Camps for children ages 4–11. Our Summer Camps offer a fun, full-immersion experience designed to encourage children to speak Italian through engaging activities such as singing, cooking, traditional games, arts and crafts, and outdoor play. Activities take place both indoors and at Battery Lane Park, located just behind the ICS main campus. Visit our Kids & Teens webpage to learn more and register. Summer Session 3 for Adults – Begins August 24 Our Summer Session 3 begins on August 24 and features three-week review courses designed to help students refresh and strengthen their Italian. We also offer a one-week Intensive Review. This is a great opportunity to build confidence, improve your skills, and preparing to join a Fall class. See our Summer Schedule here. Weekend Italian Immersion Course for Travelers Planning a trip to Italy? Our next Weekend Italian Immersion Course for Travelers takes place August 22–23, and a few spots are still available! In just one weekend, you'll learn practical Italian for real-life travel situations while gaining confidence in speaking and understanding the language. Learn more and register here. Buona estate! Francesca Casazza Executive Director & CEO REGISTER for SUMMER CAMPS  Please select Summer Camps 2026 under "Filter Programs" on the registration page       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email   Our Company | Contact Us | FAQs | Privacy Policy   The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
