Hi Dave,

You said, "by Monday." It's now Wednesday. Today's list is untouched, and the weekend is starting to look like the only way to catch up.

Ask any founder, and you'll get some version of the same story. In one study, the gap between when people expected to finish a project and when they actually finished it came to around 60%.

Nobody wants to miss a deadline, let a client down, or break another promise to the people at home. So why does it keep happening?

We've pulled together the six reasons a task takes longer than you planned, so the next time you say "Monday," it can actually be Monday.
Show me the six causes (https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=286c42bc50&e=39624a52c3)
All the best,


Barnaby
------
CEO and founder at Time etc (https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=0d5cf01db5&e=39624a52c3)
Virtual Assistants for founders
https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=20ab353f3c&e=39624a52c3

P.S. Ready to start saving time but not quite sure where to begin? Answer a few simple questions (https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=04d3dd43ec&e=39624a52c3)  and our task wizard (https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=376c3d1292&e=39624a52c3)  will set you up with personalized task ideas tailored to you and your business.
https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=bcc3e7dd1d&e=39624a52c3
https://timeetc.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=288de11005f824bb00b42b98f&id=e38205a92d&e=39624a52c3
