August Member Webinar:













Digital Risk in the Age of AI: 
Emerging Challenges for Travel Organizations
August 25, 2026 at 10am PT / 1pm ET
Join ETC members for an insightful webinar on navigating digital risk in the age of AI. Presented by Chunnie Wright, Founder of the Law Office of Chun T. Wright, PLLC, this session will explore emerging risks related to AI, privacy, cybersecurity, and online engagement, while sharing practical strategies to help travel organizations innovate with confidence.

ETC membership gives you exclusive access to live webinars, webinar recordings, member-only resources, year-round professional development, and discounted early-bird registration for the ETC Annual Conference.

APPLY FOR ETC MEMBERSHIP
















2027 Call for Conference Ideas


TheETC 2027 Conference Planning Committee invites you to help shape the conference program. Share the biggest challenges your organization expects to face over the next two to three years, submit up to three session ideas, and recommend speakers or moderators (including yourself or colleagues). Your input will help us create a timely, relevant, and engaging conference that reflects the needs of our community.
Identify your organization's key challenges.Submit up to three session ideas.Recommend speakers or moderators.
Submit your proposal by Aug 15, 2026

SUBMIT 2027 CONFERENCE SESSION IDEAS


























2027 Registration is Open


Registration is now open for the 2027 ETC Annual Conference, taking place February 21–25, 2027 in Richmond, Virginia. Reserve your spot today and join travel and tourism professionals for education, networking, and industry insights.

2027 ETC CONFERENCE INFO
