Dear Friend

Join us this Wednesday, August 5 at 7pm, for the launch of our new Hikayat series, an ongoing conversation exploring the many threads of Palestinian cultural and historical heritage.

Our first program features Haitham Khraishi, a longtime Museum docent, who will explore The Four Quartered Myth of Jerusalem: examining the history behind Jerusalem's familiar "four quarters" map and uncovering the diverse communities that have shaped the city for centuries.

Tickets are $10–$20, and we'd love to have you with us.

Reserve your spot today, we hope to see you there!

As always, if cost is a barrier, please reply to this email. We never want our programs to feel financially out of reach or exclusive, and we're happy to work with you so you can join us.

