Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Fresh, light and flavorful! THIS WEEK: THE ITALIAN R&R MENU Imagine…a glass in hand, a string quartet playing as you stroll through beautifully manicured gardens. A glass of water full of promises to enhance your well-being. The healing waters that gush from the Italian earth are drunk, soaked in and endlessly talked about. With a history of R+R that stretches back thousands of years, the Italians know a thing or two about unwinding in style. Many American spas today tout rigorous weight loss agendas, classes on meditation, and strenuous sports activities. Spas in Italy have been popular since the time of the Etruscans and Romans when they would “take the waters” in natural hot springs. They have always been a combination of exquisite spa pampering, luxurious long soaks in thermal waters to cure what ails you, and superb organic seasonal cuisine. Our offering this week takes inspiration from these spa menus of seasonal fruit, produce, and seafood, demonstrating that food can be both flavorful and healthy. Spas & Thermal Waters: 3,000 Years of R+R WEEK 331 MENU July 28 - August 2, 2026 4-COURSE MENU Nettarine, Burrata e Granturco Burrata, nectarine and corn salad Vellutata di Pomodori Arrostiti Cold roasted tomato basil soup Filetti di Sogliola ai Pinoli Fillet of sole with pinenuts and fennel potatoes Macedonia di Frutta al Maraschino Summer Maraschino fresh fruit salad Featured wine:  Tormaresca Calafuria Rose 2022 ORDER NOW!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
