There are more products being launched than ever.

That means making something good isn’t always enough.

If it looks and sounds like everything else, people will scroll straight past it.

So how do you build something people actually notice, want and remember?

Tomorrow, Roei Samuel and Atish Bhattacharjya are joining us live to talk about exactly that.

They’ll share what makes a product stand out, where people normally go wrong and how to turn an idea into something the market actually cares about.

They know what they’re talking about too.

Roei grew RealSport to 9.5 million monthly users before it was acquired. He then founded Connectd, which has helped thousands of founders connect with investors and advisors.

Atish has built products at eBay, Wish and Tripadvisor’s Viator.

Between them, they’ve seen why some products take off while others struggle to get noticed.

If you have a product, business idea or something you’re trying to bring to market, this session will help you think about it differently.

**Building A Marketplace That Pays Off**
**Tomorrow, Wednesday 29 July**

[Save your place here →](https://helpbnk.com/events/7Vl4zbqjrdprOZq)

HelpBnk 💙


