https://www.browserstack.com/webinars/aixtesting-bootcamp-hackathon-us?ref=guide-page?utm_source=livewebinar&utm_medium=email&utm_platform=&utm_content=digitalevent&utm_campaign=DevRel%20Event-11-Aug-2026-AI-X-Testing-boot-camp-US&utm_campaigncode=701OW00000wyv8UYAQ&utm_term=DevDayVirtual_APAC_ValueProp

Hi Dave,

If your team is still writing test cases by hand from PRDs and screenshots, here's what's changing for the teams that aren't:
* Test case creation, up to 90% faster AI agents read a PRD, Jira story, or screenshot and generate a structured, ready-to-run test suite, surfacing edge cases you'd normally miss.
* Zero-bloat test repositories duplicate and overlapping test cases are caught the second they're created, cutting test-maintenance overhead by up to 40%.
* Manual to automated, instantly convert manual test cases into low-code automation scripts that run across 1,000+ real browser and device combinations.

We're walking through all three, live, on August 5 then handing you 48 hours to turn what you just learned into a hackathon build.

1,200+ QA engineers and SDETs from companies like Google, Microsoft, and Atlassian have already made this shift. This session is where you catch up in one sitting, not one quarter.

You'll leave with a downloadable AI Implementation Blueprint to show your manager, an extended product trial, and if you want it a shot at the $1,500 hackathon prize pool.
See the Full Agenda & Register (https://www.browserstack.com/webinars/aixtesting-bootcamp-hackathon-us?ref=guide-page?utm_source=livewebinar&utm_medium=email&utm_platform=&utm_content=digitalevent&utm_campaign=DevRel%20Event-11-Aug-2026-AI-X-Testing-boot-camp-US&utm_campaigncode=701OW00000wyv8UYAQ&utm_term=DevDayVirtual_APAC_ValueProp)

Only 15 minutes of the 2.5 hours is a demo the rest is hands-on, in your own sandbox

Best,
The BrowserStack Team



