Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Only a few more days... GLAM IT UP IN CAPRI THIS WEEK! ﻿Right at the top of my ever growing post-COVID bucket list is a return to the Isle of Capri. It has always been a choice of well heeled international tourists and discriminating Italians. An iconic celebrity destination since the 40s and 50s, it is a glorious balance of idyllic scenery, spectacular coastline, designer shopping and fabulous homegrown flavors. Its cuisine is dominated by a plethora of fresh seafood and vegetables that are at their height now, during the summer months. This week’s menu highlights some of Capri’s most well-loved dishes paired with the region’s renowned Falanghina white wine. A Capri dinner would not be complete without a sip of its lemony nectar – limoncello – distilled right here in Washington, DC and some of the best I have ever tasted. Capri: Blue Waters & Lemon Trees WEEK 330 MENU July 21 - 26, 2026 Caponata Caprese Positano bread salad – “Fior di latte”, tomato, arugula, tuna, basil, toasted focaccia Linguine al Limone da Paolino Linguine with fresh lemon, cream, parmesan, and basil Salmone alla Mediterranea Roasted salmon filet with tomato, olives, and capers Torta Caprese Flourless chocolate almond cake Featured wine Falanghina, Feudi di San Gregorio 2020 (Read more) ORDER NOW! OUTDOOR AND INDOOR SEATING OPEN! ﻿OPEN INSIDE AND OUTSIDE EVERY TUESDAY-SUNDAY STARTING AT 4:30PM CALL 202-835-0459 TO MAKE A RESERVATION What is the Food Club? I have been feeding you in "my house" for over 30 years, and now I am here to help you feed your soul and family in YOUR home as we all adapt to this new social-distancing reality. The i Ricchi Food Club is a pre-paid pickup food service that curates authentic Italian cuisine with a pre-set 4 course menu for 2-8 people. Each week, I hand-craft a different unique dining experience that will transport you through Italy with incredible paired wines and spirits. All you have to decide is how many times a week you want to join in my culinary travels -- and I do everything else. You have enough to worry about these days. For 2 hours at your own table by the light of the provided candle, let go and let me take you on a culinary journey that I design for your nourishment and spirit. The included travel notes for those that want to have a story and learn along with their food, is my way of continuing to unite us across a common table as we all sit in our own homes. #WeAreUnited Join me in this food journey to stay connected with each other across our collective tables. #ForzaDC! LET'S TRAVEL TOGETHER! Different Membership Levels We have three Membership levels for all your needs. Trial Membership for one week is $43-$49 per person. King's Table (once per week for 4 weeks) is $34-$39 per person. An AMAZING value! Queen's Table (twice per week) is $32-$36 per person. There is something for everyone. Try it out!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
