Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.     Dear ICS Friends, This is a friendly reminder that our Latin Immersion course begins this Monday. There is still time to register—enrollment will remain open through Sunday morning. This two-week (15-hour) online immersion course is designed for teens and adults who want to learn the fundamentals of the Latin language in an intensive and engaging format. Students who complete the course will have the opportunity to continue their Latin studies in the fall and future terms with a 10-week course meeting once a week for 1.5 hours. LATIN IMMERSION – Beginners 1 Textbook: Ecce Romani 1 (Chapters 1–10) Dates: July 27 – August 7 Schedule: Monday–Friday, 6:00–7:30 pm (Online) Instructor: Annelise Brody LEARN MORE & REGISTER HERE. We would also like to remind you of our upcoming classes: OPERA LECTURE 3 (In English) Tosca, by Puccini (Wolf Trap Aug. 7) Date: Aug. 6 Thu. 6:00-8:00pm Online Diego Rodriguez COOKING CLASSES (Also available in your home!) Learn the secrets of authentic Italian cuisine from an Italian cooking teacher with a passion for food (in Italian/English). Minimum of 6 participants. Details are on our website. Dates: Sat. Aug. 15 11am-2pm & more! 16-HOUR IMMERSION COURSE FOR TRAVELERS Planning a trip to Italy? This practical weekend course will help you navigate everyday situations and communicate with confidence while traveling. Through a variety of engaging materials and videos, you'll gain the language skills you need to make the most of your Italian experience. Dates: Aug. 22-23 Sat. & Sun., 9:00am – 5:00pm Bethesda ICS KIDS Summer camps in the weeks of: August 10-14 & August 17-21 Please see the complete Summer schedule below for details, and register soon through our website to reserve your spot. ﻿ Buona estate! The ICS Team       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe 