It's Thursday. Which, if you work anywhere near London, you'll know is the real Friday now 🍻 - the office is actually full, everyone's going out tonight, and _"working from home tomorrow"_ is doing some heavy lifting.

Tonight the usual plan costs you £7 a pint standing in a crowded pub, talking about work to the people you work with.

But we’re presenting a better one… 👀

From 6 to 9PM we're taking over Bola Beach Tennis in Hackney. Real sand, Brazilian music, sunset views, and It's 26 degrees and clear skies ☀️ 

View image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/66275fd3-914e-48ce-8e33-410e6963bc6c/image.png?t=1784805119)
Caption: 

**It's £15, and that includes a drink and all your equipment.** So for the price of your first two rounds you get the whole evening being active.

Never played beach tennis? Most of Brazil hadn't either until a couple of years ago - the sport went from 400,000 players to over a million there in two years, because anyone can rally within minutes of picking up a bat.

👉[SAVE MY SPOT →](https://bolabeachtennis.as.me/schedule/51a04503/?appointmentTypeIds[]=95092579)

-HelpBnk


