If you're having trouble viewing this email, you can see it online, https://api.neonemails.com/emails/content/ATDvF5jwhqFcRhJ1eQRduFysA2MvORHPMov7O4vw1aw=.
Hi Friends,

I'll say it every year and I'll keep saying it: this is my favorite weekend of the year. We're just 3 days away from our third annual Museum of the Palestinian People Art and Culture Festival: Rooted in Resistance, Here Eternally and there's nothing quite like watching our community come together to celebrate and honor the joy, beauty, and resilience of being Palestinian.

We're kicking things off on Friday, July 24 (7pm) at The Festival Center with our Kick-Off Dinner, an evening of Palestinian food (catered and sponsored by Kanoon), art, and performance featuring a moderated panel with Palestinians across industries, plus live music from Mohammad Karzon, Fairouz Foty, and Ayah Helmy. It's an intimate night that always ends up being one of my favorite moments of the whole weekend, and proceeds go directly toward supporting MPP's mission. 

We have limited seats left, so please book your spot today:

Reserve Your Seat for Friday Here! 

Then Saturday, July 25 (12–6:30pm), we open the doors to everyone for the main Festival day at The Festival Center: a full day of art, culture, and community. And this year, Saturday is extra special: we're also hosting an Open House at the Museum with a live silent art auction, debuting our newly expanded space, made possible entirely because of MPP supporters like you. I can't wait to finally show you all what your support has built.

RSVP for Saturday Here!

I hope to see you all this weekend! If you have any questions or if cost is a barrier, please reply to this email, and I'm happy to help! 

With you, always, 

Leah

And a huge thank you to our sponsors as this Festival would not be possible without them: 

Palestinian American Medical Association 

Falafel Inc. 

Kanoon

Al Ard 

Anera



 



Support MPP Monthly



 



Follow Our Instagram

