Last chance to sign up for member only webinar!
Building for AI Discovery July 23rd, 2026
REGISTRATION IS REQUIRED


There's still time to join ETC and register for our upcoming member-exclusive AI webinar on July 23. AI is changing how travelers discover organizations online. Join Susan Black, founder of Wowzitude, to learn practical strategies for increasing your organization's visibility in AI-powered search, creating AI-friendly content, and measuring your AI presence.


Can't attend live? No problem. The webinar will be recorded and available on demand in the ETC Resource Library for members.

An ETC membership includes access to exclusive webinars and recordings, member-only resources, professional development opportunities throughout the year, and discounted early-bird registration for the ETC Annual Conference

APPLY FOR ETC MEMBERSHIP




2027 Call for Conference Session Ideas
TheETC 2027 Conference Planning Committee invites you to help shape the conference program. Share the biggest challenges your organization expects to face over the next two to three years, submit up to three session ideas, and recommend speakers or moderators (including yourself or colleagues). Your input will help us create a timely, relevant, and engaging conference that reflects the needs of our community.
Identify your organization's key challenges.Submit up to three session ideas.Recommend speakers or moderators.Let us know if presenting is required for your organization's conference travel approval.
Submit your proposal by Aug 15, 2026

2027 Call for Conference Session Ideas




Registration Is Open for the 2027 ETC Annual Conference
February 21-25, 2027 in Richmond, VA


Registration is open for the 2027 ETC Annual Conferencein Richmond, Virginia! Join colleagues from across the educational travel community for engaging educational sessions, meaningful networking, and opportunities to exchange ideas and best practices.

The ETC Annual Conference is a members-only event, so attendees must have an active ETC membership to register. If your membership has lapsed, now is the perfect time to renew and reconnect with the ETC community.

An ETC membership provides year-round value through professional development, industry insights, networking opportunities, exclusive member resources—including our members-only job board—and discounted conference registration.




Former Members: We'd love to welcome you back. Contact us to renew your membership.
New to ETC? Apply today and discover the benefits of being part of our growing educational travel community.

APPLY FOR NEW ETC MEMBERSHIP
This email was sent on behalf of Educational Travel Consortium located at 27 NE 55th Ave, Portland, OR, 97213.To unsubscribe click here. If you have questions or comments concerning this email contact Educational Travel Consortium at etc@educationaltravelconsortium.com.



