Choosing an attribution model is a technical decision, not just a marketing one. It determines your data infrastructure requirements, partner transparency demands, and switching costs down the line.

We published a detailed breakdown of the six major attribution models—what each one requires technically, which partners respond to which models, and why most programs choose wrong the first time.

Also covers the blind spots most programs have: only 20% of brands track CAC by partner, and only 18% track AOV by partner. That gap means you're optimizing for volume, not growth.

Worth reading if you're evaluating affiliate programs or thinking about what proper tracking infrastructure actually looks like.

