Email from Bridges to Independence Impact All Summer Long     Hi David, Halfway through summer, Bridges to Independence is celebrating a season filled with growth, learning, and community connection.  Scroll down below to see how Bridges is spending the summer!   BACK TO SCHOOL Our annual Back-to-School Drive is underway, helping ensure that every child we serve starts the school year equipped for success. Community members, businesses, and supporters can help by donating school supplies that will be distributed to local children and families. Donations will be accepted through August 16, and supporters are encouraged to contribute supplies that help students feel confident and prepared on their first day back in the classroom. We're also excited to partner with Scramble Indoor Play! Customers who bring a school supply donation to Scramble will receive 20% off purchases at the café and $5 off admission. Full List of School Supplies   END-OF-SUMMER FUN FEST About Before the school year begins, we’re celebrating summer with two exciting days of family fun! Stop by Scramble Parkour in Shirlington for a day of play. This event is a wonderful opportunity to gather with friends, enjoy the final days of summer, and support Bridges to Independence. 📅 August 6 & 7 📍 Scramble Parkour, 2900 S. Quincy St, Arlington VA 22206   HIGHLIGHTS FROM SUMMER CAMP Summer is flying by at our Thrive & Shine Summer Camp! We have already completed the first half of camp, where youth have enjoyed a variety of enriching activities. Highlights have included pool days, rock-climbing adventures, and visits to local parks and museums. One of the most memorable experiences has been our "Around the World Week." Campers created their own passports and embarked on a journey of cultural discovery, learning about countries, traditions, and customs from across the globe. Through hands-on activities and interactive lessons, youth expanded their understanding of the world while celebrating the diversity that makes our communities strong. As we reach the midpoint of the summer, we are grateful for the opportunity to provide a safe, supportive, and engaging environment where children can create lasting memories! OUR BRIDGES' FAMILY This summer, we have been truly blessed by the support of our community who have stepped forward to help families achieve self-sufficiency. Whether you donated supplies, volunteered your time, organized an event, or shared our mission with others, your support is creating pathways to independence for children and families. If you would like to learn more about how you can help families move from homelessness to stability, please reach out to info@bridges2.org. Thank you for being part of the Bridges family.   July 2026   DONATE         Bridges to Independence | 2229 Shirlington Road, Suite B | Arlington, VA 22206 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Our Privacy Policy | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
