Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.     Dear ICS Friends, As Summer Session 2 continues, there are still plenty of opportunities to learn with us before Session 3 begins on August 24. We are pleased to highlight the following upcoming courses: LATIN IMMERSION Beginners 1 for Teens and Adults. This two-week (15-hour) immersion course is for beginners who want to learn the fundamentals of the Latin language. Textbook: Ecce Romani 1 (ch. 1-10) Dates: July 27 - Aug. 7 Online Mon.-Fri., 6:00-7:30pm Annelise Brody  OPERA LECTURE 3 (In English) Tosca, by Puccini (Wolf Trap Aug. 7) Date: Aug. 6 Thu. 6:00-8:00pm Online Diego Rodriguez COOKING CLASSES (Also available in your home!) Learn the secrets of authentic Italian cuisine from an Italian cooking teacher with a passion for food (in Italian/English). Minimum of 6 participants. Details are on our website. Dates: Sat. Aug. 15 11am-2pm & more! 16-HOUR IMMERSION COURSE FOR TRAVELERS Planning a trip to Italy? This practical weekend course will help you navigate everyday situations and communicate with confidence while traveling. Through a variety of engaging materials and videos, you'll gain the language skills you need to make the most of your Italian experience. Dates: Aug. 22-23 Sat. & Sun., 9:00am – 5:00pm Bethesda ICS KIDS Summer camps in the weeks of: August 10-14 & August 17-21 Please see the complete Summer schedule below for details, and register soon through our website to reserve your spot. ﻿ Buona estate! The ICS Team       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
