Hi Dave,

If you could look at a hundred successful founders' to-do lists, the most interesting thing wouldn't be what's on it, but what's missing from it.

The average founder loses around 36% of their working week (https://www.timeetc.com/resources/how-to-achieve-more/the-big-price-of-small-tasks-how-entrepreneurs-may-be-unwittingly-keeping-their-businesses-small/) to routine admin tasks, so we wanted to see how Time etc users are tipping the balance back in their favor.

We dug into 1,500 tasks assigned to VAs over the course of a month, and the same things kept showing up again and again. We've rounded them all up in our latest article.

Every task on this list is one less thing on somebody else's plate, and quite possibly still on yours. 
Show me the list (https://www.timeetc.com/resources/how-to-use-a-virtual-assistant/15-ways-real-founders-use-their-virtual-assistant-to-finally-feel-on-top-of-things)
All the best,


Barnaby
------
CEO and founder at Time etc (https://timeetc.com/ref/institute)
Virtual Assistants for founders
https://timeetc.com/ref/mailchimp

P.S. Ready to start saving time but not quite sure where to begin? Answer a few simple questions (https://www.timeetc.co.uk/get-started-wizard)  and our task wizard (https://www.timeetc.co.uk/get-started-wizard)  will set you up with personalized task ideas tailored to you and your business.
https://www.facebook.com/trytimeetc
https://www.twitter.com/timeetc/
https://www.linkedin.com/company/time-etc-limited

============================================================
