Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Plus, a special dinner honoring Thomas Jefferson next Wednesday, 7/22. Not to miss! IF YOU AREN'T AT THE BEACH THIS WEEK...WHY NOT EAT LIKE YOU ARE? With 5000 miles of coastline, Italy has the most beaches in Europe. Nowhere in Italy are you more than two hours from a beach. Italians absolutely love beach life and are, most likely, the sexiest and most fashionable beachgoers in the world. La Versilia is a very unique stretch of Tuscan Mediterranean coast backed by the Apuan Alps. It is best known for its golden beaches, nightlife, art communities, and surf-n-turf – Mare e Monti – cuisine. But to fully enjoy the Italian beach culture you need to know its unspoken rules. After all, you do not want to look like a tourist on an Italian beach! Tutti al Mare! Tuscans at the Beach WEEK 329 MENU July 14-19, 2026 Zucchini Grigliati e Burrata Smokey grilled zucchini ribbons, soft burrata cheese, parsley breadcrumbs and saba Risotto Gamberetti e Bietola Imported Vialone Nano rice, shrimp, swiss chard and parmesan Scaloppine di Pollo ai Funghi Chicken breast scaloppini with white wine reduction, wild mushrooms, and fresh herbs Bomboloni Tuscan donuts filled with vanilla cream and dusted with sugar Featured wine Vernaccia di San Gimignano, Teruzzi e Puthod, 2022 ORDER NOW! SPECIAL DINNER! ONE NIGHT ONLY WEDNESDAY, JULY 22, 2026 For those enjoying the 250th anniversary of our beautiful country, we have put together an evening to delight both your mind and your taste buds. Thomas Jefferson was an avid traveler and brought both ideas and food to the US from Europe. Join Jefferson Hotel DC historian Susan Sullivan Lagon with Chef Christianne Ricchi as they draw inspiration from the foods of eighteenth-century Tuscany and Virginia to honor the exchange of culture that helped shape the American nation. This is a night not to be missed! MORE INFO HERE SAFELY-SPACED OUTDOOR AND INDOOR SEATING NOW OPEN! ﻿OPEN INSIDE AND OUTSIDE EVERY TUESDAY-SUNDAY STARTING AT 4:30PM CALL 202-835-0459 TO MAKE A RESERVATION What is the Food Club? I have been feeding you in "my house" for over 30 years, and now I am here to help you feed your soul and family in YOUR home as we all adapt to this new social-distancing reality. The i Ricchi Food Club is a pre-paid pickup food service that curates authentic Italian cuisine with a pre-set 4 course menu for 2-8 people. Each week, I hand-craft a different unique dining experience that will transport you through Italy with incredible paired wines and spirits. All you have to decide is how many times a week you want to join in my culinary travels -- and I do everything else. You have enough to worry about these days. For 2 hours at your own table by the light of the provided candle, let go and let me take you on a culinary journey that I design for your nourishment and spirit. The included travel notes for those that want to have a story and learn along with their food, is my way of continuing to unite us across a common table as we all sit in our own homes. #WeAreUnited Join me in this food journey to stay connected with each other across our collective tables. #ForzaDC! LET'S TRAVEL TOGETHER! Different Membership Levels We have three Membership levels for all your needs. Trial Membership for one week is $43-$49 per person. King's Table (once per week for 4 weeks) is $34-$39 per person. An AMAZING value! Queen's Table (twice per week) is $32-$36 per person. There is something for everyone. Try it out!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
