Email from ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation From groundbreaking research grants to inspiring stories of courage and community, hope continues to grow. $4.2 Million Invested in New Research The ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation, together with its partners, is proud to announce a $4.2 million investment in nine new DIPG/DMG research projects over the next three years. Together, these projects tackle some of the most pressing challenges in the field, from precision medicine and combination therapies to next-generation immunotherapy and treatment resistance, while accelerating promising discoveries toward pediatric clinical trials. With this latest commitment, the foundation has now invested more than $48 million in 112 researchers across 50 institutions worldwide, further strengthening its position as the world's leading private funder of DIPG/DMG research and accelerating the search for more effective treatments. ﻿ Learn how these groundbreaking projects are advancing the future of DIPG/DMG research and bringing us one step closer to a cure. Read More SHINE WITH IZZY: WHERE MAGIC MEETS HOPE Just weeks before starting pre-kindergarten, Izzy Cashion was enjoying a carefree summer filled with princesses, unicorns, and dreams of the adventures ahead. Then, a devastating DIPG diagnosis changed everything. With her signature blonde curls, bright blue eyes, and unbreakable spirit, Izzy is touching countless people through her courage and resilience as she faces one of the deadliest forms of childhood cancer. Read how Izzy's remarkable journey is inspiring hope and helping drive the search for a cure. Meet Izzy POWER OF PARTNERSHIP Tower Companies is a wonderful example of what can happen when a committed partner brings people together around a shared mission.. Through their support of the ChadTough Defeat DIPG Superhero Sprint & 6K, they inspired others to join the fight.﻿ ﻿ By inviting tenants, employees, contractors, and business partners to participate, they created a ripple effect of awareness and support for children battling DIPG. What began as one company's commitment has grown into hundreds of participants coming together each year to honor Michael Mosier's legacy. Keep Reading Upcoming Events Mark your calendars for these 2026 events that benefit ChadTough Defeat DIPG! More information about each event will be released as it becomes available. July 27 — Chicago Golf Outing Foursomes are sold out, but you can still join us for dinner, drinks, and raffles! | Riverside, IL August 13 — Whitecaps Rivalry Night Show your U-M or MSU pride at this game to benefit a great cause! | Comstock Park, MI September 20 — Emerson the Brave Stampede 5K Fun Run & Color Run | Holland, MI September 27 — RunTough is back! Participants can enjoy the 5K, 1M Fun Run, and more for an afternoon of family fun! Virtual options available and early bird rate ends after July 31 | Saline, MI November 10 — Sparkle & Shop Luncheon | Lathrup Village, MI November 26 — Ann Arbor Turkey Trot 5K & 1M Fun Run on Thanksgiving morning | Ann Arbor, MI Make a Monthly Donation! Your support will fund game-changing DIPG/DMG research and provide one-on-one help to families battling DIPG and DMG. Are You a Thrivent Member? Through Thrivent Choice®, you can support ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation by directing Choice Dollars® or making a personal donation — with Thrivent covering the processing fees. It’s a simple way to make an even greater impact in the fight against DIPG/DMG.           ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation | PO Box 907 | Saline, MI 48176 US Unsubscribe | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
