    Employer Newsletter- July 2026
  



 

  

    
  



 

  

    Towson University—Summer in Photos
  



 

  

    From orientations to arts festivals, camps and more, summer brings a new rhythm to TU’s campus. Read on for a few of the highlights of summer 2026 so far.
  



 

  

    
      
        More Summer in Photos
      
    
  



 
 
 

  

    Fall 2026 Recruitment Opportunities
  



 

  

    2026 Part-Time & On-Campus Job Fair
Wednesday, August 26 • 3–5 p.m. • UU Ballrooms
Need to hire some great part-time employees? This fair allows you to meet, interview and hire TU students to fill your part-time, short-term and seasonal positions!
  



 

  

    
      
        Register for Part-Time Job Fair
      
    
  



 

  

    Plug Into Tech InternshipsThursday, September 17 • 3–5:30 p.m. • 7800 York Road
This fair connects employers with students pursuing Computer Information Systems and related technology fields. Register for a great opportunity to recruit internship talent in areas such as data analytics, cybersecurity, software development, IT consulting, and business technology while engaging with motivated students preparing for careers in tech!
  



 

  

    
      
        Register for Plug Into Tech Internships
      
    
  



 

  

    2026 Actuarial Science and Risk Management FairFriday, October 2 • Noon–3 p.m. • UU Ballroom A
This event connects employers with students interested in actuarial science, risk management, insurance, finance, analytics, and related career paths. Employers will have the opportunity to promote internships and full-time roles, build brand awareness, and connect with students preparing for careers in risk-focused industries.
  



 

  

    
      
        Register for ASRM Fair
      
    
  



 

  

    Fall 2026 Career & Internship Fair
Friday, October 16 • 11 a.m. – 2 p.m. • SECU Arena
With more than 1,000 students from all majors expected to attend, this is your opportunity to meet motivated candidates seeking full-time roles, internships, and early career opportunities.
  



 

  

    
      
        Register for Career & Internship Fair
      
    
  



 

  

    Fall 2026 Marketing, Media, and Communication ExpoTuesday, November 3 • 5-7 p.m. • UU Ballroom E
A boutique fair specially designed for students interested in learning more about internships and career paths related to the marketing, media and communication industries.
  



 

  

    
      
        Register for Expo
      
    
  



 

  

    Fall 2026 Careers in Care FairTuesday, November 10 • 3:30–5:30 p.m. • UU Ballroom D 
Careers in Care is a boutique recruiting and engagement event designed to connect employers with TU students interested in mental, community, and behavioral health, individual and family support services, and holistic well-being. This targeted fair provides organizations with the opportunity to promote open roles and internships, share their mission and impact, and build early relationships with students preparing for summer internships and fall employment.
  



 

  

    
      
        Register for Careers in Care Fair
      
    
  



 

  

    Power Pitches Speed NetworkingMark your calendar – November 12
