Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Discover the extraordinary friendship between Tuscan patriot Philip Mazzei and Thomas Jefferson—and how their shared ideas helped influence the founding ideals of the United States.   Experience an unforgettable evening of history, inspiration, and discovery as we explore the extraordinary relationship between America's Founding Father, Thomas Jefferson, and Philip Mazzei—a remarkable Tuscan Renaissance thinker whose influence on the birth of the United States has largely been forgotten. Prepare to be surprised by one of history's best-kept secrets. WEDNESDAY, JULY 22, 2026 Did you know..... "The great doctrine 'All men are created equal,' incorporated into the Declaration of Independence by Thomas Jefferson, was paraphrased from the writings of Philip Mazzei, an Italian-born patriot and close friend of Jefferson's. (John F. Kennedy "A Nation of Immigrants")   RESERVE YOUR SPOT!     Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
