"The harder you work, the luckier you get."

It's a LIE! 

It's sold to you by people who need you working hard until you die. Nurses work hard. Police work hard. Hours in _does not_ equal value out.

What actually builds wealth is EQUITY. 

Owning a piece of something worth pouring yourself into. The gap between selling an hour of your time and owning a percentage of something is not a small difference. It's the game many are playing that don't want you to know.

Most people never think to ask for equity inside the job they already have. But don't just ask for a slice of the business. Go to your employer and tell them what you'll deliver over the next few years. Ask for a percentage of the company if you hit it. _Vested equity_ tied to results is a conversation most employers respect.

And if they won't have it? Consider if moving jobs or setting up your own is your next move.

Simon built Fluid from zero and sold it to PwC. Below is 15 things he wished he'd known in his 20s and 30s. Find the 'Get Equity Where You Work' section. Worth every minute.

👉 [Watch it free here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CdYPTATcTeM)

– HelpBnk

P.S. Stop asking what am I earning and start asking who owns the upside of what I'm doing. Same hours. Same effort. Completely different destination.


———

