<tr><td align="

The best performance drug in the world makes you sharper, better looking, and more productive. It's completely FREE and most founders are voluntarily skipping it every night.

It's sleep! 

And most people aren't burnt out. They're just chronically under-rested.

Here’s what you need to know. Deep sleep happens in the early part of the night. Miss it by staying up late and you can't get it back by sleeping longer in the morning. Whatever fun gets sacrificed in the name of a good night's sleep, we'll leave that between you and your partner _wink, wink_

View image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/003f136b-f67e-4562-98d2-4386b803864e/image.png?t=1782249538)
Caption: 

Brian Johnson is the king of sleep. He holds the record for the best sleep scores recorded on Whoop. Eight straight months of perfect sleep. 

One change worth trying tonight: eat your last meal two to three hours before bed. Why? It lowers your resting heart rate, which directly improves sleep quality, which directly improves willpower and decision-making the next day. It costs nothing.

Sleep is the only performance variable that's completely free and compounds every night you get it right.

We sat down with Brian, who spent over $4 million understanding his own biology, to find out how to perform at your best while building a business. The answer wasn't hustle harder.

👉 [Watch Bryan Johnson's 3 Steps To Fix Your Tiredness](https://youtu.be/9SavNBwhIj8?si=VLZd6B7G6NQ5Rl3m)

– HelpBnk

P.S. Brian goes to bed at 8:30pm. We're not saying go that far. But a consistent routine might surprise you.


