      <table style="width: 100%; font-family: 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentat

Simon built Fluid from nothing into one of the most successful marketing agencies in Asia. Then sold it to PwC for more money than he will ever need.

The reason it sold? It didn't need him to run it.

Most founders building right now are accidentally building themselves a job. Every client relationship runs through them. Every decision needs their sign-off. Every process lives in their head. It feels like being indispensable. The reality? It's a trap.

David, if you sold one part of your business tomorrow, would it still function?

Not the whole thing. Just one piece. The way you onboard a client. How complaints get handled. Your sales process. If you said "only if I'm there," that's exactly where to start. Write it down. Hand it to someone. See what breaks.

Post your biggest bottleneck in the HelpBnk community. Founders there have either solved it or are figuring it out alongside you.

​​==👉 ==[[Join thousands of entrepreneurs building smarter for FREE on HelpBnk]](https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.6gGTtSqytZvjrOWiXlYoU1iOj3NZQQVVSP1Vlq2ZKxslUy2CDCHpASMkYc_OLxa07vfBF3UznJXsenj3CWMbvm13yWzV0iZThVutsqsdGBvdsIeQeGZyMprENBXqjuYApirAlvsnMGtR9JRDGv5gRRJOMJzdvJtP9OPCOtdGXRqZSVW6U8rCmaiAeXbjGcAM_l6Qa7ogFVYmc26t90fJiw/4of/KW3d1STdRyC3a_2vBaR1TA/h0/h001.yjad2pYaYELNUDzSh5FLNVdk1AzBE3JGwSk32nd1lOo)

– HelpBnk

P.S. The business that needs you for everything isn't a business. It's a 24h job.


