Dear Friend, 

Time is almost up. You have until July 10th to confirm your spot in the Suleiman Al-Obeid Legacy Soccer Tournament on July 26th as an individual or as a full team.

The World Cup is in full swing right now. Palestine has no team on the pitch and yet we have been ever-present throughout this tournament. Egyptian fans have flown the Palestinian flag high in the stands. Moroccan players have proudly held it up after their matches. Norway's team has spoken out for Palestine on one of the world's biggest stages. Sumud, steadfastness, shows up everywhere, even where we're not officially present. 

And still, Israel continues to target Palestinian soccer players. Just last week, Palestinian goalkeeper Saleem Al-Ashqar was killed in Gaza.

This is why the Suleiman Al-Obeid Legacy Soccer Tournament matters. This tournament is for everyone but it is especially for every player who can no longer take the field. We play for Suleiman Al-Obeid. We play for Saleem Al-Ashqar. We play in solidarity, and we play for them.

Join us on July 26th as part of MPP Festival Weekend for a day of soccer, community, and sumud.

[Register Now]

We hope to see you on the field.

Register for the Soccer Tournament!



 



Support MPP Monthly



 



Follow Our Instagram

