Everyone's having a meltdown about AI.

Half the internet thinks it's the apocalypse. The other half thinks one prompt will make them a millionaire by Thursday.

But what can AI structurally NOT do?

It can't build the same quality relationships you built because you got burnt by the wrong people. It can't give you the judgment that only comes from making that terrible decision at 2am. It can't hand you the thing that actually makes founders dangerous: the** PROCESS.**

Goldman Sachs says 300 million jobs will disappear. Is this a reason for panic? No. Because being adaptable and proactive will take you further in this tech gold rush than your job ever could.

The businesses that win won't be the ones who use AI the most. They'll be the ones built around things AI can't touch. Your story, your community, your trust.

Simon Sinek has spent 20 years studying what makes humans successful. His TED Talk has 60 million views. What he says about what makes humans irreplaceable is worth 10 minutes.

👉 [Watch Simon Sinek's full take here](https://youtu.be/W2a_adkjqiA?si=LcAB179RDvSUElDZ)

– HelpBnk

P.S. The founders who win the AI era won't be the best prompters. They'll use AI together with everything they've learnt the hard way.


