Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Learn the secrets of Sardinian centenarians :) Plus, our contribution to America 250... ﻿This week: Sardinia here we come! The most interesting fact about the island of Sardinia is that it boasts the largest number of centenarians per capita than any other place on Earth. Their consumption of clean, simple “peasant food,” together with red wine rich in antioxidants and polyphenols just may be the reason for their longevity. Our Sardinian menu highlights the mainstays of their Mediterranean diet – legumes, vegetables, olive oil, pasta, cheese and seafood. Those together with, Cannonau, a red wine made from grapes indigenous to the island could be the key to living a long and healthy life. Sardinia: Where People Live Forever WEEK 328 MENU July 7-12, 2026   Insalata di Ceci, Tonno e Ruchetta  Chickpea and tuna salad with arugula Malloredus alla Campidanese  Sardinian gnochetti with pork ragu and Sardinian pecorino cheese Spiedino di Mare  Marinated shrimp skewers with sweet peppers and red onions Torta Sarda di Ricotta  Sardinian lemon ricotta tart Featured wine: Cantina di Mogoro, Nero Sardo, Cannonau di Sardegna DOC, 2023 ORDER NOW!   COME BY AND SEE US IN PERSON TOO! OPEN EVERY TUESDAY THRU SUNDAY STARTING AT 4:30PM CALL 202-835-0459 TO MAKE A RESERVATION What is the Food Club? I have been feeding you in "my house" for over 30 years, and now I am here to help you feed your soul and family in YOUR home as we all adapt to this new social-distancing reality. The i Ricchi Food Club is a pre-paid pickup food service that curates authentic Italian cuisine with a pre-set 4 course menu for 2-8 people. Each week, I hand-craft a different unique dining experience that will transport you through Italy with incredible paired wines and spirits. All you have to decide is how many times a week you want to join in my culinary travels -- and I do everything else. You have enough to worry about these days. For 2 hours at your own table by the light of the provided candle, let go and let me take you on a culinary journey that I design for your nourishment and spirit. The included travel notes for those that want to have a story and learn along with their food, is my way of continuing to unite us across a common table as we all sit in our own homes. #WeAreUnited Join me in this food journey to stay connected with each other across our collective tables. #ForzaDC! LET'S TRAVEL TOGETHER! Different Membership Levels We have three Membership levels for all your needs. Trial Membership for one week is $$59 per person. King's Table (once per week for 4 weeks) is $44-$49 per person. An AMAZING value! Queen's Table (twice per week) is $42-$46 per person. There is something for everyone. Try it out!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
