Rory Sutherland has spent 30 years at Ogilvy shaping how people feel about brands like American Express and Dove, and his whole career has been built on one question: why do people actually buy? 

He used champagne to explain something that trips up a lot of founders.

Champagne isn't really selling you a drink. It's selling you permission to say that this moment is worth marking properly, which is exactly why the cheaper bottle that tastes nearly identical still doesn't feel right. You were never paying for the taste.

Here's why that matters for your business.

When your price looks too low, the customer doesn't think "bargain." They think "what's wrong with it?" They won't tell you that. They just won't buy. You'll refresh your analytics wondering what happened, and the honest answer is: your price talked them out of it before they even read the rest.

The price is part of the product. And right now, yours might be working against you.

Rory sat down with Simon and shared $22,381 worth of marketing advice. FREE.

👉 [Watch Rory Sutherland's $22,381 Marketing Advice for FREE](https://youtu.be/ecR1Sd0q3lE?si=nfrh-24kUcAKawWr)

– HelpBnk


