🎆 Getting to Fourth of July Celebrations 🎆
Fourth of July in the District is one of the most anticipated events of the year, drawing thousands of visitors from near and far to celebrate in the nation's capital. With massive crowds expected, traffic becomes a major headache, and navigating road closures and limited parking options can quickly turn excitement into frustration.

Help your guests get to the festivities with ease by sharing our 2026 Fourth of July on the National Mall Guide (https://godcgo.com/wp-content/uploads/Getting-to-the-Fireworks-Guide.pdf) .
This guide provides your guests with all the ways they can get to the National Mall conveniently and sustainably whether by Metro, scooter, bike, or bus. Download our guide and provide it to your guests when checking in so they'll know the easiest ways to travel to and from these popular events.

DOWNLOAD THE GUIDE (https://godcgo.com/wp-content/uploads/Getting-to-the-Fireworks-Guide.pdf)
goDCgo is your #1 resource for transportation information and options to make getting in and around DC easier than ever. An initiative of DDOT (District of Department of Transportation), goDCgo provides visitors, residents and employees with the education and assistance they need to make informed choices about traveling in the District.
