Friends,

This month, we gather once again in Washington, DC for the Museum of the Palestinian People's third annual art and culture festival.

Our theme this year is:

Here Eternally | هنا إلى الأبد Rooted in Resistance | متجذر في المقاومة

We invite you to begin the weekend with our Opening Night Dinner, an evening designed to nourish both body and spirit through food, conversation, and music.
Friday Opening Night

Join us for a special catered dinner generously sponsored by Kanoon Smokehouse, celebrating the richness and resilience of Palestinian cuisine. 

The evening will feature a thoughtful panel discussion with distinguished Palestinian voices, including a psychologist, an acclaimed author, and a journalist, who will reflect on storytelling, resilience, memory, and the role of Palestinian voices across industries in this historic moment.

We'll close the evening with live musical performances celebrating the  creativity and enduring spirit of Palestinian culture.

Secure your spot for Friday here. 

Throughout the weekend, festival attendees can also experience:

• A curated Palestinian Souq featuring local artisans and small businesses
• Palestinian film screenings
• Children's programming and storytime
• Zine-making, tatreez, and hands-on art activities
• Palestinian food vendors
• A community soccer tournament
• The unveiling of the Museum of the Palestinian People's new museum space

We hope you'll join us as we celebrate what has always sustained our people: our culture, our community, and our unwavering commitment to one another.

RSVP for Saturday Here

SUNDAY, JULY 26 - THE SULEIMAN AL-OBEID LEGACY CLASSIC

Join us for the 1st Annual Suleiman Al-Obeid Legacy Classic Soccer Tournament. Suleiman Al-Obeid, known as the Pele of Palestinian Football, played 24 international matches for the Palestinian national team and scored over 100 goals in his career. He was killed in Gaza while waiting for aid in August 2025. Nearly one year since his death, this tournament is intended to bring together community from across the East Coast and the DMV to honor the legacy of Al-Obeid and all Palestinian athletes who can no longer play. 

Register Your Team or as an Individual Player!

We are looking forward to seeing you all in Washington D.C. next month! 

MPP Team 



 





 



Support MPP Monthly



 



Follow Our Instagram

