Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Plus a special ONE NIGHT ONLY dinner and history talk that will BLOW your mind This week in the Food Club: Another week of culinary travels -- this time accompanied by the entrancing writings of Frances Mayes. This year marks 55 years (yikes!) since I saw the Tuscan sun for the first time. I can clearly remember that first morning in the little pensione on Via 27 Aprile when I flung open the shutters to discover the most vivid colors, sparkling clean air, and brightest sun I had ever seen. Tuscany is a region located in central Italy but ask any Tuscan and they will tell you it is the center of the universe. They are exceedingly proud of their heritage and are profoundly connected to their culture, not the least of which is their culinary patrimony. Our menu this week will travel through the region, highlighting specialties from its different provinces. We are also introducing a little-known light Tuscan red wine, Sabazio, that is best enjoyed lightly chilled, to “temperatura di cantina.” Under the Tuscan Sun WEEK 327 MENU June 30-July 5, 2026 (closed 7/4) Bruschetta ai Peperoni Rossi Sweet red peppers and black olives ‘melted’ with Balsamic vinegar Pici all’Aglione Thick homemade spaghetti with tomato, garlic and whipped ricotta Costata di Maiale al Genepro e Salsa di Susine Roasted rack of pork with juniper berries and fresh plum sauce Bietola Saltata Sautéed swiss chard with garlic and EVOO Zuppa Inglese ai Frutti di Bosco ‘English Soup’ trifle with vanilla custard and summer berries Featured wine La Braccesca, Sabazio, Rosso di Montepulciano 2021 (Read more) ORDER NOW! OUTDOOR AND INDOOR SEATING NOW OPEN! ﻿OPEN INSIDE AND OUTSIDE EVERY TUESDAY-SUNDAY STARTING AT 4:30PM CALL 202-835-0459 TO MAKE A RESERVATION What is the Food Club? I have been feeding you in "my house" for over 30 years, and now I am here to help you feed your soul and family in YOUR home as we all adapt to this new social-distancing reality. The i Ricchi Food Club is a pre-paid pickup food service that curates authentic Italian cuisine with a pre-set 4 course menu for 2-8 people. Each week, I hand-craft a different unique dining experience that will transport you through Italy with incredible paired wines and spirits. All you have to decide is how many times a week you want to join in my culinary travels -- and I do everything else. You have enough to worry about these days. For 2 hours at your own table by the light of the provided candle, let go and let me take you on a culinary journey that I design for your nourishment and spirit. The included travel notes for those that want to have a story and learn along with their food, is my way of continuing to unite us across a common table as we all sit in our own homes. #WeAreUnited Join me in this food journey to stay connected with each other across our collective tables. #ForzaDC! LET'S TRAVEL TOGETHER! Different Membership Levels We have three Membership levels for all your needs. Trial Membership for one week is $43-$49 per person. King's Table (once per week for 4 weeks) is $44-$49 per person. An AMAZING value! Queen's Table (twice per week) is $42-$46 per person. There is something for everyone. Try it out!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
