Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.     Dear ICS Friends, Summer Session 2 begins on July 6, with a wide selection of in-person and online Italian courses for Beginner, Intermediate, and Advanced students. Whether you are just starting or looking to refine your skills, our classes offer a welcoming environment to learn, practice, and connect with fellow Italian language enthusiasts. As our two-week intensive courses come to a close, Session 2 introduces a new One-Week Intensive Review (Monday–Friday) for Elementary and Intermediate students—a perfect opportunity to refresh and strengthen your Italian in just one week. For those beginning their Italian journey, Beginner 1 is offered in two convenient formats: Online: once a week In person (Bethesda): twice a week In addition to our language courses, explore Italy through our special cultural offerings. This summer you can learn about Sicily, discover current events with Italy Today, admire the art of Palazzo Barberini, or prepare for the upcoming opera Eugene Onegin by Tchaikovsky, and Tosca by Puccini. Please note that Latin Immersion 1 (Teens & Adults) has been rescheduled and will now take place July 27–August 7. Looking ahead, don't miss our popular 16-Hour Italian Immersion for Travelers on August 22–23. This practical weekend course provides the essential language and cultural skills to help you travel around Italy with greater confidence and enjoyment. Please see the complete Summer schedule below for details, and register soon through our website to reserve your spot. ﻿ Buona estate! The ICS Team       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
