Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.       Dear Music and Opera Lovers, We are delighted to invite you to an upcoming lecture exploring one of the most beloved works in the Italian operatic repertoire: The Listener’s Guide to Tchaikovsky’s Eugene Onegin Lecture with Diego Rodriguez Thursday, July16 | 6:00–8:00 PM Online via Zoom Prepare for Wolf Trap Opera’s presentation of Eugene Onegin with a special online lecture exploring the music, characters, and emotional depth of Tchaikovsky’s beloved masterpiece. Discover how Tchaikovsky transformed Alexander Pushkin’s celebrated novel in verse into one of opera’s most moving works. Through an exploration of the story, characters, and score, participants will gain insight into the poetry, passion, and musical brilliance that define Eugene Onegin. Whether you are new to opera or a seasoned enthusiast, this lecture will provide valuable context and a fresh listening perspective before attending Wolf Trap Opera’s production of Eugene Onegin. On our Music School webpage, you can find the program of our opera’s lectures and purchase tickets without additional fees, through our registration page . Performances take place at The Barns at Wolf Trap on July 17, 19, 23, 25, 2026. Please register by Wednesday, July 15, at 5:00 PM. A Zoom link will be sent to online attendees approximately 30 minutes before the lecture begins. Contact p.vera@italianculturalsociety.org if you have any questions. We look forward to sharing this musical journey with you! Get your tickets today! Registration details are available on our website under: UPCOMING EVENTS The ICS Team.       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email   Our Company | Contact Us | FAQs | Privacy Policy   The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
