Lily saved $3,000 working at a care home.

She had no business experience. No nepo baby connections. No plan beyond "I made a candle, and my mum said she'd buy it."

So she put it on a Shopify site she'd built in an afternoon, priced it at $5.99, and her mum bought it. (The world’s most reliable first customer.)

Then a friend bought one. Then she cold-messaged her local gym asking if she could set up a pop-up. They said yes. She made $850 in a single day.

She didn't need an elaborate business plan. She just kept asking the next person.

Simon sat down with her to break down the exact steps she took from that first $5.99 sale to a $5k/month business, and how to scale to $10k.

👉 [Watch Simon Explain How To Get Your First $5k/month](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xu_Hpqz0pgQ&t=18s)

-HelpBnk

**P.S.** Lily's now got a studio in her garden, just hired someone, and is finally paying herself properly. It all started with a candle kit from Amazon. You can get there too.


