 &zwnj; 
 

ADL D.C.'s collaboration with jewish security professionals


 &zwnj; 
 


 &zwnj; 
 


Antisemitic incidents and threats against the Jewish community have surged to unprecedented levels, making proactive security and community collaboration more critical than ever. That is why this month, ADL D.C. was proud to partner once again with 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxd5QRrD4S2LvQXGBFY85uq-DWK9p9spefWQ1PnqcIo9y255P6WuYSPyRdTTBnfBqMTIsXtZ7pks6vpb1Me1JS1qh5NqIJT 
JShield  for a briefing on our 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxeIwoxUUvlT0zzaQY5M7ZzTqdEEF8edjh3QZspxJbGtS_zUabArJUP6YlAbUfMeH--nd6ctJyJ2vxfudp7RKYFLEz3uYC9 
2025 Audit of Antisemitic Incidents , the importance of community members reporting those incidents, and how we can work together to protect Jewish life. This event is just one part of our ongoing partnership with JShield, through which we continue to build stronger, more resilient communities equipped to identify, report and combat antisemitism.


If you have experienced an incident of antisemitism, extremism, bias, bigotry or identity-based hate or discrimination, you are not alone. Report an incident to ADL by 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxfc0YYJb7v_k0Y5r_vjgLL6EtAhJQu_2RJvJLFp5kygBojbPLnBg6r3Ms-NZPV2qRFHb-o0Yj-JJ666Z7EjPGmF_mFZVG7 
clicking here. 


 &zwnj; 
 


 &zwnj; 
 

ADL D.C. teaming up with toli


 &zwnj; 
 


 &zwnj; 
 


This month, as part of an ongoing partnership, ADL Washington D.C.'s Regional Coordinator joined educators at the Capital Jewish Museum through 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxg3Rtn0PoPQF-DhfTy4NsEHa1SFxpdrudq4tv0kj9HpZq_-beX_AXIppbc8FU5lR7xXIVnLAZQRtUK1ez2Q541Ley5K1iw 
The Olga Lengyel Institute (TOLI)  to unpack how antisemitic narratives take root and how K-12 teachers can challenge them in their classrooms and communities.


Equipping educators with the tools to recognize and challenge antisemitism is essential to building safer, stronger communities. Thank you to TOLI for the partnership and for fostering these critical conversations.


 &zwnj; 
 


 &zwnj; 
 

what is the true crime community (tcc)?


 &zwnj; 
 


 &zwnj; 
 


The True Crime Community (TCC) is a disturbing online subculture whose members harbor a dangerous fascination with serial killers and mass murderers, often creating dark memes and fan fiction that glorify violent criminals and their crimes. 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxhOy9iojcwULWWvR4IgdI6mBhID0804onMy0H11wkeovd97UalsotKRWVZbsKyJS29LKaLcSyU8mAbnHMe-XZZ1cpefKkj 
ADL's Center on Extremism  has found that multiple recent school shooters were active participants in TCC spaces, where violent content increasingly overlaps with white supremacist ideology, antisemitism and extremist radicalization. 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxiSWC1GPhVONOGwCbbHJG5paZY0IzaNkJ65mmq3Yx_Q0W6US819RhlqedwID1onTNRFP4TNDenHfnK1CWtueSoFiyLoh6K 
ADL's new backgrounder breaks down what TCC is, why it matters and what parents, educators and community members need to know to recognize and address this threat. 
https://click.adlmail.org/?qs=ABB7InYiOjEsImQiOjQ5MTl9AAEAAAAAAOjPnfxjN-TL25ksxKeyzGmGPfe51LL8rtG148_tPKeiTeUWi1T8cOZ1bAnqaqAbHDJ6JytdbqfxS3zP-tctaXzk8nPEck4TXEPd 
Click here to read. 


