Save the Date · Saturday, October 17, 2026 · Washington National Cathedral · SOME's 39th Annual Break the Cycle Gala.  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌

Mark your calendars for  SOME's 39th Annual Break the Cycle Gala [https://give.some.org/event/somes-annual-break-the-cycle-gala/e789039] on Saturday, October 17, 2026, at the Washington National Cathedral. This special evening brings our community together to raise critical funds for individuals and families experiencing poverty and homelessness in Washington, DC, while celebrating the resilience and achievements of those we serve.

2026 Gala Co-Chairs             Kevin Keane President & CEO,

American Beverage Association    Kenny Roberts Principal,

Invariant

Our Co-Chairs bring distinguished leadership, generous service, and a shared commitment to strengthening communities. Through their professional achievements and dedication to creating opportunity for others, they embody the spirit of Break the Cycle and the values at the heart of SOME's mission.

2026 Honorees           Jim McCarthy   Father Horace McKenna

Humanitarian of the Year Award     Dennis & Pam Lucey   Father John Adams Legacy Award     Marriott Foundation   Champion Partner Award           Reserve Your Table & Sponsorship [https://give.some.org/event/somes-annual-break-the-cycle-gala/e789039]

To learn more about sponsorship opportunities and reserve your table or purchase tickets, use the button above. To get involved with the Gala or explore other ways to partner with SOME throughout the year, contact  Lee Granados [mailto:leegranados@some.org] or review our  Partnership Umbrella Deck [https://some.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/SOME_UmbrellaDeck_2025.pdf].

We look forward to seeing you on October 17!

So Others Might Eat · 71 O Street NW, Washington, DC 20001

