Email from Ristorante i Ricchi Dinner, gladiators and virgins What a week in Florence! Join the festivities from afar as this magical city celebrates its feast day - San Giovanni - and learn about the city's bitter rivalries and the sweet elixirs brewing. June is a wonderful month to visit Florence. It is a month when pagan and Christian rites combine to celebrate colorful sporting events, Renaissance parades, and ancient culinary traditions. Calcio Storico is a well-kept Florentine secret; Medieval-style soccer played in typical Renaissance garb. Think rugby meets cage-fighting with pantaloons. Not only does June 24th mark the birthdate of Florence’s patron saint, John the Baptist, but it is also the day to harvest soft green walnuts to make the spicy “digestivo,” Nocino. (Read Chef Christianne's Travel Notes this week to see how virgins fit in.) Florentine cuisine today is earthy and rustic much like it was at the time of the Renaissance. The “Trattoria” is the keeper of these culinary traditions, the equivalent of Nonna’s cooking. Our menu this week highlights the typical Florentine dinner you might eat at our trattoria in Cercina. Florence in June: Bitter Rivalries & Sweet Elixirs WEEK 326 MENU June 23-28, 2026   Antipasto Fiorentino  Florentine Antipasto – Prosciutto and Finocchiona fennel salami with Tuscan melon Ribollita  Hearty vegetable soup “reboiled” (ribollita) with Tuscan bread and parmesan cheese Rosticciana  Grilled marinated pork ribs alla Toscana served with green beans stewed in tomato Salame Dolce  Sardinian lemon ricotta tartSweet “salami” – chocolate crunch with walnuts and Chantilly cream Featured wine Villa Antinori Rosso 2020, Super Tuscan ORDER NOW! BEAUTIFUL GARDEN OUTDOOR SEATING NOW OPEN! ﻿OPEN INSIDE AND OUTSIDE EVERY TUESDAY-SUNDAY STARTING AT 4:30PM CALL 202-835-0459 TO MAKE A RESERVATION   What is the Food Club? I have been feeding you in "my house" for over 30 years, and now I am here to help you feed your soul and family in YOUR home as we all adapt to this new social-distancing reality. The i Ricchi Food Club is a pre-paid pickup food service that curates authentic Italian cuisine with a pre-set 4 course menu for 2-8 people. Each week, I hand-craft a different unique dining experience that will transport you through Italy with incredible paired wines and spirits. All you have to decide is how many times a week you want to join in my culinary travels -- and I do everything else. You have enough to worry about these days. For 2 hours at your own table by the light of the provided candle, let go and let me take you on a culinary journey that I design for your nourishment and spirit. The included travel notes for those that want to have a story and learn along with their food, is my way of continuing to unite us across a common table as we all sit in our own homes. #WeAreUnited Join me in this food journey to stay connected with each other across our collective tables. #ForzaDC! LET'S TRAVEL TOGETHER! Different Membership Levels We have three Membership levels for all your needs. Trial Membership for one week is $43-$49 per person. King's Table (once per week for 4 weeks) is $34-$39 per person. An AMAZING value! Queen's Table (twice per week) is $32-$36 per person. There is something for everyone. Try it out!   Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email #PayItForward Give the gift of a beautiful meal Perhaps it's a friend's birthday, your parent's anniversary, a small kind gesture to a needy neighbor, teacher or priest to show you are thinking of them. Food nourishes the soul and our curated menus and travel notes will give them a special experience completely different from your average take-out. Ristorante i Ricchi | 1220 19th Street NW | Washington, DC 20036 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
