Hi Dave,
* Jeff Bezos won't touch his to-do list before 10 a.m.
* Warren Buffett has lists of goals he's committed to ignoring.
* Richard Branson doesn't do anything that someone else could do better.

Unpack these choices and the pattern is hard to miss: every one of them found a way to make sure their best hours stayed theirs.

We’ve pulled nine of these habits together in one piece, with what each founder learned and what you can apply right now. The Buffett prioritization method alone is worth the read.

The full breakdown, including what Zuckerberg's five-word mantra can do for your momentum, is in the article.

What would your week look like if you applied even two of them?
Read the nine habits (https://www.timeetc.com/resources/how-to-achieve-more/9-rules-for-life-from-the-worlds-most-successful-entrepreneurs/)
All the best,


Barnaby
