Email from ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation Meet a remarkable young man, explore promising research advances, and see how supporters are turning awareness into action. A Spirit That Won't Quit At 18 years old, Daniel Childress has already faced more adversity than most people encounter in a lifetime. After experiencing concerning symptoms during his senior football season, Daniel and his family embarked on an unexpected journey that ultimately led to a DMG diagnosis.﻿ ﻿ What followed was a relentless search for hope, a high-risk surgery, and a determination that continues to inspire everyone around him. Through every setback, Daniel has remained focused on moving forward with courage, optimism, and an unwavering belief that there is no such thing as losing. For Daniel, making progress is the only solution.﻿ ﻿ Read Daniel's story and discover how one young man's resilience is inspiring a community and reminding us all what it means to keep fighting. Read Daniel's Story RESEARCH SPOTLIGHT: PRATEEK THENGE Behind every research breakthrough is a reason to keep searching for answers.﻿ ﻿ Meet one of the ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation's Predoctoral Fellows, who is using cutting-edge immune cell engineering to develop new ways to fight DIPG/DMG. His work may happen one experiment at a time, but each step brings us closer to better treatments, and more hope, for children facing this devastating disease.﻿ ﻿ Read how your support is helping transform progress and possibility. Learn More RUNNING WITH PURPOSE Five Upper St. Clair High School students recently took on the Pittsburgh Marathon Relay in honor of their friend, Sam Levine, who passed away from DIPG in December 2025. Competing as team "The Lumberjacks," they transformed their grief into action, raising awareness and inspiring others through a message Sam embodied every day: the strength to keep going, even when the journey is difficult. Read how Sam's courage and enduring legacy continue to propel them forward — one mile, and one meaningful step, at a time. Keep Reading Upcoming Events Mark your calendars for our 2026 events! More information about each event will be released as it becomes available. September 20 — Chicago Golf Outing Foursomes are sold out, but you can still join us for dinner, drinks, and raffles! | Riverside, IL September 20 — Emerson the Brave Stampede 5K Fun Run & Color Run | Holland, MI September 27 — RunTough is back! Participants can enjoy the 5K, 1M Fun Run, and more for an afternoon of family fun! (Virtual option available) | Saline, MI November 10 — Sparkle & Shop Luncheon | Lathrup Village, MI November 26 — Ann Arbor Turkey Trot 5K & 1M Fun Run on Thanksgiving morning | Ann Arbor, MI Make a Monthly Donation! Your support will fund game-changing DIPG/DMG research and provide one-on-one help to families battling DIPG and DMG. Are You a Thrivent Member? Through Thrivent Choice®, you can support ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation by directing Choice Dollars® or making a personal donation — with Thrivent covering the processing fees. It’s a simple way to make an even greater impact in the fight against DIPG/DMG.           ChadTough Defeat DIPG Foundation | PO Box 907 | Saline, MI 48176 US Unsubscribe | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
