Email from Bridges to Independence A Season of New Beginnings     Hi David, Yesterday marked the first official day of summer! At Bridges, summer is one of our most exciting times of year, as our youth are out of school and engaging in new opportunities every day. There are plenty of ways to stay active and connected this season. Scroll down below to see how Bridges is spending the summer!   STEP UP TO THE PLATE Our Annual Kickball Tournament returns! The tournament has become one of our most popular events each year, and we look forward to another exciting day of community spirit and friendly competition. Learn More 📅 Saturday, August 8th at 8AM 📍 Gunston Park, 1401 28th St S 👥 Teams of 10–15 players welcome 🎯 All skill levels encouraged 🤝 Registration closes July 27th   UNITED IN MOVEMENT Register We are excited to provide a FREE, safe, and encouraging environment where young athletes can play soccer together. Whether your child is new to soccer or already loves the game, everyone is welcome to join the fun. 📅 Saturday, June 27 🕗 10:30 AM - 12:30 PM 📍 Charles Drew Field 😄 Ages 4+ About Before the school year begins, we’re celebrating summer with two exciting days of family fun! Stop by Scramble Parkour in Shirlington for a day of play. This event is a wonderful opportunity to gather with friends, enjoy the final days of summer, and support Bridges to Independence. 📅 August 6 & 7 📍 Scramble Parkour, 2900 S. Quincy St, Arlington VA 22206   FATHER'S DAY REFLECTIONS "For this Father’s Day, I’ve been reflecting deeply on what being a father has meant in my own life. Of all the roles I hold - CEO, leader, advocate, community member - being a father is the one that has shaped me the most. Fatherhood has brought some of the greatest joy and purpose I have ever experienced. It has also humbled me. Becoming a father changed the way I see responsibility, love, sacrifice, and legacy. It made me realize that children do not need perfection - they need presence. They need someone who shows up consistently, who listens, who guides, who protects, and who loves unconditionally. Like many fathers, I have had moments where I questioned whether I was doing enough, providing enough, or leading well enough. But over time, I’ve learned that some of the most meaningful moments are often the simplest ones - conversations at the dinner table, laughter during ordinary days, showing up for important milestones, or simply being there during difficult moments. Those are the moments children remember. Those are the moments that build trust, security, and love. My work at Bridges to Independence has only deepened my appreciation for fatherhood. I meet fathers who are carrying enormous burdens while still fighting to create better futures for their children. I see fathers working long hours, overcoming setbacks, rebuilding their lives, and continuing to show incredible resilience and love for their families. Their strength inspires me constantly. Fatherhood has taught me that true leadership begins at home. It is not about titles or recognition - it is about character, consistency, compassion, and the example we set every day. The values we model as fathers often become the foundation our children build their lives upon. This Father’s Day, I am grateful - grateful for my family, for the privilege of being a father, and for the reminder that some of life’s greatest successes are not measured by professional accomplishments, but by the relationships we nurture and the love we give to those closest to us. To all fathers and father figures in our community: thank you for continuing to show up, even when life is hard. Your presence matters more than you know." Fraser Murdoch, CEO, Bridges to Independence   BACK TO SCHOOL DRIVE While summer vacation has just begun, we're already preparing for the upcoming school year. Our annual Back-to-School Drive is underway, helping ensure that every child we serve starts the school year equipped for success. Community members, businesses, and supporters can help by donating school supplies that will be distributed to local children and families. Donations will be accepted through August 16, and supporters are encouraged to contribute supplies that help students feel confident and prepared on their first day back in the classroom. Full List of School Supplies   June 2026   DONATE         Bridges to Independence | 2229 Shirlington Road, Suite B | Arlington, VA 22206 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Our Privacy Policy | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
