      <div style="display: none;">A post about Food featured on Travel Massive. &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &zwnj;
      &#160;&#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &zwnj;
      &#160;&#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; &#847; </div>

    <div role="article" aria-roledescription="email" aria-label="" lang="en">
      <table style="width: 100%; font-family: 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation">
        <tr>

Every founder hits a point where they feel stuck.

Growth slows down.

The next hire feels impossible.

Fundraising isn't going to plan.

You're working harder than ever, but not seeing the results you'd hoped for.

**That's why we're excited to be hosting a live session with Roei Samuel.**

Roei built and scaled RealSport to millions of monthly users before successfully exiting the business. Today, as Founder & CEO of Connectd, he's helped thousands of startups connect with investors, advisors, and experienced operators who can accelerate growth.

He's seen firsthand what separates the businesses that break through from the ones that stay stuck.

And now he's joining us live, TOMORROW.

### During the session, we'll discuss:

* The biggest growth challenges founders face today

* Common mistakes that hold businesses back

* How successful founders think differently

