Hi there,

This is the last note about the free 30‑minute Brand Gameplan. Ten days from today, it goes back to $199.

If Mangia Food Tour (launched October 08, 2013 was the spark, this is the part where we add direction. One short call with an expert—no slides, no pitch—and you walk away with a plan that makes the next ten customers easier to win.

What you get, right after the call:

* A 1‑page 90‑day plan with 2–3 next moves in the right order
* Rough timelines & budget ranges so you can act with confidence
* A quick consistency checklist for your top channels

Reply with two times you’re available (and your time zone). I’ll lock it in.

Not into meetings? Two other easy wins

1) Essential Branding Toolkit (+ $134 savings inside)

Short, practical tools to keep your brand tight, plus $134 in project savings ($35 off + free $99 Advanced Promotion), ready when you start your next project.

Get the Toolkit and my $134 discount: https://assets.crowdspring.com/marketing/landing-page/guides/crowdspring-essential-branding-kit-ver-1-0.zip

2) 48‑Hour Express Audit (no call)

Reply AUDIT with one link or screenshot (homepage, menu, flyer, post). We’ll reply within 48 business hours with three fixes you can implement this week.

Whichever path you choose—talk to a human, use the Toolkit, or get a quick audit by email—you’ll leave with a clearer next step. If you want the free 1:1, this is the week.

Thanks,

Marc Boyle
Head of Customer Support and Success

P.S. Last chance for the free session before it returns to $199. If you’re on the fence, reply with one link you want me to assess and I’ll send one idea you can use this week.


Use the following link to unsubscribe from these types of emails: https://www.crowdspring.com/bb/unsubscribe/f232ac96ebc64cdd831e875f6a267df8/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=bb&utm_campaign=wb6%2Bmths.<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml"><head>
