Meet the Makers: A Cool-Climate Tasting Featuring Wines From Mendocino Ridge & Santa Cruz Mountains With the Owners of Trail Marker

[Bachelet](https://sf.vervewine.com/collections/verve-san-francisco-wine-tastings/products/hella-chenin-tasting-event-wednesday-may-20th-5-7pm-pt)

Journey through two of California's most compelling cool-climate wine regions, Mendocino Ridge and the Santa Cruz Mountains, as we explore how elevation, fog, and the Pacific Ocean influence every glass.

Drew Huffine and Emily Virgil, owners of Trail Marker, will guide us through an unforgettable tasting spanning vintages from 2021 to their newest releases.

The high elevations and strong Pacific influence of these appellations produce longer growing seasons and lower yields, resulting in freshness, vibrant acidity, and mountain-grown concentration. If you're a fan of Burgundy or Oregon wines, this tasting is for you. Paired with light bites.

Date: Wednesday, June 24thTime: 5:00 - 7:00 PM PTLocation: Verve Wine SF, 2358 Fillmore St, San Francisco, CA 94115Ticket Price: $35 per personFeatured Lineup:

-

Trail Marker Wine Co Mendocino Chardonnay Manchester Ridge Vineyard 2021

-

Trail Marker Wine Co Mendocino Rose of Carignan 'Bartolomei Vineyard' 2025

-

Trail Marker Wine Co 'Petites Joies' Trousseau 2023

-

Trail Marker Wine Co Santa Cruz Mountains Pinot Noir 2023

Guarantee your tickets now!

