Hello,



My name is Samantha "Sam" Carrico, and I am the Supervisor for The Body Safety Program<https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/familyservices/children-youth/volunteer-partner-services/body-safety/volunteers> within the Fairfax County Department of Family Services. This free program gives children a comfortable, non-alarming way to talk about the sensitive and complex problem of child abuse and is run entirely by volunteers.



I am reaching out because we are hosting a training on Thursday, August 27th at 11:00am for 60 of our dedicated volunteers.
As part of our training, we will be raffling off themed baskets to our volunteers to show our gratitude for all that they do for the vulnerable children they help protect. We were hoping you would be willing to donate a free cooking class for our raffle baskets to support our event and help make it successful.
If you can donate, please let me know how we can coordinate.

I have attached our W-9 for your information.



Thank you for your consideration and support.

Thanks,

Samantha "Sam" Carrico, LCSW
Volunteer and Partner Services Supervisor
Facility Dog Handler for Rylynn<https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/familyservices/children-youth/rylynn-the-facility-dog-life-at-the-department-of-family-services>
Want to Give Back?<https://a.co/hrO9Lpp>
Child Abuse & Neglect Prevention Program
12011 Government Center Parkway│Fairfax, VA│22035
Office: 703-324-7576
Cell: 571-536-8192
samantha.carrico@fairfaxcounty.gov<mailto:samantha.carrico@fairfaxcounty.gov>
