Dear Friend

We warmly invite you to join us this Saturday, June 13, from 7-9pm at the Museum of the Palestinian People for the opening reception of From Lily's View, an exhibition honoring the life and photography of Lily Bandak.



In 1948, the course of life would be altered forever for the Palestinian people in one of the most transformative and traumatic periods in Palestinian history. Lilly Bandak was born just a few weeks following, in Amman, Jordan. 

Bandak would later confront her own challenges being diagnosed with multiple sclerosis, limiting her mobility and freedom of movement. Neither Palestine nor Bandak confined themselves to be defined by loss. 

This exhibition highlights resilience as an adaptation and to not be defined by circumstances that have been imposed. Just as Palestinians continue to build lives, communities, and preserve cultural and historical heritage despite displacement and fragmentation, Bandak refused to allow physical limitations to determine her place in the world.

We are honored to be spotlighting Bandak's work in our space. A few details about our opening night: 

Date: Saturday, June 13

Time: 7-9pm

Light refreshments and snacks will be served. 

We hope to see you there! 

