Navigating travel disruptions is a growing part of a travel advisor’s day-to-day work. From weather events and wars to fuel shortages and shifting regulations, the backdrop against which travel is sold keeps shifting. Through it all, advisors are expected to provide what clients need most: peace of mind.

But what about
the advisors themselves?

In this video series, Open Jaw looks at how to manage the added pressure, uncertainty and anxiety that come with selling travel in a world in flux.

VIDEO SERIES NOW PLAYING!

Thank you for submitting your questions and comments. Hear them addressed in our personal wellness discussion, now playing.

Rocky Racco and Nina Slawek address how world events are challenging advisors, blurring the line between travel planning and crisis management.

Risk management expert, Tyler Hosford, of International SOS provides practical advice on managing uncertainty in a rapidly shifting global landscape.

The conversation shifts to managing our own anxiety as we move from one travel disruption to the next, while navigating client expectations. With special guest Tamar Ishaky, Registered Therapist.

Click to visit page (https://openjaw.com/videos/training/crisis-management-video-series/)

