Email from The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C.     Dear ICS Friends, On Saturday, June 6th, from 11:00 am to 2:30 pm in McLean, Virginia, Ornella will welcome you into her home for a cooking class and guide you through the preparation of three delicious Italian recipes: Mini piadine ripiene di prosciutto e formaggio – Mini piadinas stuffed with ham and cheese: a dish that is perfect both as an appetizer and as a main course. Piadina -originally from Emilia-Romagna- is one of the most versatile staples of Italian cuisine, and in this class, we will prepare it with extra-virgin olive oil. Polpette al limone – A delicate and flavorful variation of the famous Italian meatballs, enhanced with the fresh taste of lemon. Biscotti ferro di cavallo – A classic Italian cookie found in bakeries and pastry shops throughout Italy. These delicious treats are shaped like horseshoes and finished with chocolate-covered tips. Please register by tomorrow, Friday, June 5, at 12:00 p.m. by selecting "Cooking Classes" on the registration page. Visit our website to learn more about this and upcoming culinary events. Buon appetito! The ICS Team       Share This Email Share This Email Share This Email   Our Company | Contact Us | FAQs | Privacy Policy   The Italian Cultural Society of Washington D.C. | 4833 Rugby Ave Suite 201 | Bethesda, MD 20814 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Contact Data Notice<!DOCTYPE HTML>
