Dear Friend

We're growing our team and we'd love your help spreading the word. We are currently hiring for two exciting positions: 

Communications Intern
We are seeking a passionate and creative Communications Intern to support the Museum's communications and programs teams. This is a wonderful paid Summer (12 weeks) opportunity for an aspiring communications/digital media professional who is deeply passionate about cultural advocacy, design, and storytelling. Candidates are required to be located in the greater Washington D.C. area. 

Preferred Start Date: June 15; applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. 

Job Description & Application Instructions

GIS QA & Application Specialist, Bayt wa Balad Project
Bayt wa Balad, the Museum's Mellon Foundation-funded project, seeks a GIS QA Specialist to analyze prototype testing feedback, refine the interface based on team input, prepare a summary report with recommendations, and establish testing protocols. The specialist will provide experienced, human-led analysis informed by GIS best practices. Candidates in the Washington, DC area are preferred but not required. This hourly contract position runs through August 31 and requires approximately 80–100 hours of work. 

Preferred Start Date: July 1; applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. 

Job Description & Application Instructions

We welcome applicants from all backgrounds who are passionate about preserving and sharing Palestinian history, culture, and identity. 

If you have any questions about either position, please don't hesitate to reach out to us at jobs@mpp-dc.org we'd love to hear from you.

With gratitude, 

MPP Staff

